      "note": "At each eligible eight-bar phrase of a full passage (never its first, which plays the skeleton whole) one family, then one variant: continue; subtract (the drums open the end of the phrase and the bass completes a glide across the gap, or a kick taken out of bar four); answer (the end of bar four or eight changed: the turnaround, a ghost pickup with the bass resting under it, an accent moved); support-change (the one auxiliary part enters for one or two phrases with its exit planned, or the open hat lifts over the phrase's second half); effect (one backbeat or rim throw, after the place's own end throw is checked). A fill plays only into a change, and the bass rests under it. features: what each of a form's return features plays. stateVariants: the kit state a track plays where its form asks a state, drawn once a track (each a kit state). developed: a full passage the form marks for development (broken-air) leans to answers and subtractions, and the track's edit vocabulary (drawn once, off the form's features.edits) multiplies its variants' weights.",
